language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ A hiker chooses which items to put in a backpack of limited capacity, maximising the total value of the items taken.
given capacity : int(0..10000)
given weights : matrix indexed by [int(1..5)] of int(0..10000)
given values : matrix indexed by [int(1..5)] of int(0..10000)
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..5)] of bool
find total : int(0..50000)

branching on [x]

maximising total
such that
$ the total weight of the items taken must not exceed the capacity of the backpack
(sum i : int(1..5) . x[i] * weights[i]) <= capacity,
$ the total value is the sum of the values of the items taken
total = (sum i : int(1..5) . x[i] * values[i])
